lions, and plots, as well as the ambitions and demands of the Lancastrian retainers who had helped him win the throne. By 1406 his rule was broadly established, and although he became ill shortly after this and never fully recovered, he retained ultimate power until his death. Using a wide variety of previously untapped archival materials, Chris Given-Wilson reveals a cultured, extravagant, and skeptical monarch who crushed opposition ruthlessly but never quite succeeded in satisfying the expectations of his own supporters.","pageCount":621,"publicationYear":2016,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"Biography & Autobiography","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-henry-iv-chris-given-wilson"}],"displaySummary":"This comprehensive and nuanced biography restores to his rightful place a king often overlooked in favor of his illustrious progeny. Henry faced the usual problems of usurpers: foreign wars, rebellions, and plots, as well as the ambitions and demands of the Lancastrian retainers who had helped him win the throne. By 1406 his rule was broadly established, and although he became ill shortly after this and never fully recovered, he retained ultimate power until his death. Using a wide variety of previously untapped archival materials, Chris Given-Wilson reveals a cultured, extravagant, and skeptical monarch who crushed opposition ruthlessly but never quite succeeded in satisfying the expectations of his own supporters.","primaryTopic":"Family Biography","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"History","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"History","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"History","mappedSubject":"History","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book 'Henry IV' by Chris Given-Wilson primarily focuses on historical events and figures related to the life and reign of Henry IV, making 'History' the appropriate primary subje